vulkan: round the alpha test reference to 1/255 in the pipeline key (off by default)

Core patch. Paths are the submodule's. Applies on core16 alone.

Source: Frizti/Lichii ec3a455c6f by zortos293, a port of Djihads80/Eglantine#544 (9b603f53a7).

EDEN_NX2_ALPHA_REF_ROUND=1. Titles that fade with the alpha test on move the reference by less than
one 8-bit step a frame, and each value is a new pipeline. The PR measured 925 to 101 pipelines built
in a Fire Emblem scene on PC. Rounding keeps one pipeline per step textures can tell apart. The
threshold moves by at most half a step.

Why here: a pipeline costs pool memory and a stall on the console. Ocarina's own count is unknown.

Changed from the source: off by default, there always on.

Runs on the PS5: same core path.
Hang: none. Keys change while it is on, so pipelines stored with unrounded values build once more.
Pool memory: none added; fewer pipelines if the game fades this way.
Checked: applies on core16. PS5-target syntax compile, no errors. 2 million reference values: 256 keys,
rounding twice changes nothing, largest shift exactly half a step. Not run on the console.

Co-authored-by: zortos293 <65777760+zortos293@users.noreply.github.com>

diff --git a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/fixed_pipeline_state.cpp b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/fixed_pipeline_state.cpp
--- a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/fixed_pipeline_state.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/fixed_pipeline_state.cpp
@@ -5,6 +5,8 @@
 // SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later
 
 #include <algorithm>
+#include <cmath>
+#include <cstdlib>
 #include <cstring>
 #include <bit>
 #include <numeric>
@@ -184,10 +186,18 @@
     // The reference is part of the pipeline only while the test compares with it: title 1
     // animates the register with the test off (text fading in and out), which made a new
     // pipeline, translated on the GPU thread, for every value (~84% of its runtime pipelines).
+    // EDEN_NX2_ALPHA_REF_ROUND=1: titles that fade with the test on move the reference by less
+    // than one step of 8-bit alpha a frame: one pipeline per step the textures can tell apart.
+    static const bool round_alpha_ref = [] {
+        const char* const value = std::getenv("EDEN_NX2_ALPHA_REF_ROUND");
+        return value != nullptr && value[0] == '1';
+    }();
+    const float alpha_ref = round_alpha_ref ? std::round(regs.alpha_test_ref * 255.0f) / 255.0f
+                                            : regs.alpha_test_ref;
     const u32 packed_alpha_test = alpha_test_func.Value();
     alpha_test_ref = packed_alpha_test != PackComparisonOp(Maxwell::ComparisonOp::Never_GL) &&
                              packed_alpha_test != PackComparisonOp(Maxwell::ComparisonOp::Always_GL)
-                         ? std::bit_cast<u32>(regs.alpha_test_ref)
+                         ? std::bit_cast<u32>(alpha_ref)
                          : 0;
     point_size = std::bit_cast<u32>(regs.point_size);
 
